==Enemy==
Elizabeth the LVIth has high health but relatively low damage and range. Additionally, she has a 100% chance to produce a Lv.3 [[Wave Attack]] on hit, so she will punish the player for spamming meatshields, as those Waves can reach much further than herself and whittle down anything not immune to it.

==Strategy==
When first encountered in ITF1 [[New York (Into the Future)|New York]], Elizabeth is best confronted with durable units, but not meatshields. Examples include rangers like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] as well as melee units like [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]] and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]]. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]] is decently bulky and can rush in without getting knocked back, allowing his Anti-Alien Freeze ability to potentially activate, stopping her from attacking.

If you are fighting [[Cli-One]] or [[Corrupted Valkyrie]] in Into the Future's [[Moon (Into the Future)|Moon]] stages, Elizabeth's appearance will spell certain defeat unless a helpful uber at hand neutralizes either the boss or herself.

After Into the Future, Elizabeth becomes pretty easy to deal with because she has somewhat low range and damage for a [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave Attacker]]. Players are also likely to acquire [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave-immune]] or even [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield units]], completely nullifying the only threat she poses. It will be especially hard for her to deal with a stream of [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cats]].

